    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Prefix compression: given a sorted list of keys that share a common prefix, store the prefix once and keep only the unique suffixes.</para>
<para>Example: Input: [&quot;idx:users:country:USA:pk1&quot;, &quot;idx:users:country:USA:pk2&quot;, &quot;idx:users:country:USA:pk3&quot;] Result: prefix = &quot;idx:users:country:USA:&quot;, suffixes = [&quot;pk1&quot;,&quot;pk2&quot;,&quot;pk3&quot;] </para>
    </detaileddescription>
